course: dictionary
lesson: 6917
title: Breaking down a long word
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A long word can look scary, but its context often gives you clues. You can also check whether the word has parts you already know. «Pachycephalosaurus had a bony dome up to 25 centimetres thick.» The words bony dome and thick tell you this dinosaur had a very thick head.
explain: Its name means «thick-headed lizard», which matches the clues. Pachy means thick, cephal means head, and saurus means lizard. Always ask: what does the sentence say about it? Then try your meaning in the sentence instead of the hard word and see if it still makes sense.
explain: Some clues tell you what people are unsure about. «Scientists argue whether it head-butted like goats.» Argue means they disagree. The word whether shows they are not yet sure what the dome was for, so the text is asking a question, not giving a final answer.
fact: Context means the words and sentences around a word.
fact: «Pachycephalosaurus» was a plant-eating dinosaur with a very thick, dome-shaped skull.
fact: It lived in North America about 66 million years ago.
fact: Its name means «thick-headed lizard».
fact: «Argue» means to disagree, and «whether» shows that people are not yet sure.
exercise: «Pachycephalosaurus had a bony dome up to 25 centimetres thick.» What is the dome part of? | The feet | The tail | *The skull | The teeth
exercise: Was Pachycephalosaurus a meat-eater or a plant-eater? | Meat-eater | Fish-eater | *Plant-eater
exercise: «Scientists argue whether it head-butted like goats.» What does argue mean? | *Disagree about something | Agree completely | Sleep soundly | Run very fast
test: Pachycephalosaurus lived in North America about how many years ago? | 660 years | 66 thousand years | *66 million years | 6 million years
test: «Some domes have healed injuries, which supports the head-butting idea.» What does supports mean here? | Breaks | *Gives evidence for | Hides | Measures
exam: Why might scientists think Pachycephalosaurus head-butted others? | Because it lived in water | *Because some domes show healed injuries | Because goats told them so | Because it had no head at all
